Q: Avoid a lot of conditions inside an If Statement A: <p>In javascript, if you add true and true together you get 2. Using this information you could put all the conditions in an array and get the sum of it.</p>

<pre><code>var conditions = [condition1, condition2, ... ]; -- all conditions go here

var sum = 0; -- works out the sum
for (var i = 0; i &lt; conditions.length; i++) {
    sum += conditions[i];
}

if (sum === conditions.length) {
    console.log("success")
}
</code></pre>

Q: React layout help - Can&#39;t get my SVG&#39;s to be a set size while also responsive A: <p>Specify width for each svg tags.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;svg1 id="svg1"&gt;
&lt;svg2 id="svg2"&gt;

#svg1 {
  position: absolute;
  top: 40%;
  left: 50%;
  width: 400px;
  transform: translate(-50%,-50%);
}

#svg2 {
  position: absolute;
  top: 60%;
  left: 50%;
  width: 300px;
  transform: translate(-50%,-50%);
}
</code></pre>

Q: Displaying Different Images React A: <p>well with javascript you can do it like this:</p>

<pre><code>import React from "react";
import image1 from "./img/1.png";
import image2 from "./img/2.png";
import image3 from "./img/3.png";

const imageArray = [image1, image2, image3];

const App = () =&gt; {
  const [current, setCurrent] = React.useState(0);

  React.useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const timerId = setInterval(() =&gt; {
        setCurrent(cur =&gt; (cur &lt; imageArray.length - 1 ? cur + 1 : 0));
    }, 500);
    return () =&gt; {
        clearInterval(timerId);
    };
  }, []);

  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
        &lt;img src={imageArray[current]} alt="img" /&gt;
        {current}
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
};
export default App;
</code></pre>

Q: How to add a Loading Animation when a Button is Clicked? A: <p>I took your code and modified it just a little bit to achieve your desired result (based on what I understood from your question).</p>

<pre><code>class App extends Component {
  state = { fadingOut: false };
  fadeOut = () =&gt; this.setState({ fadingOut: true });

  render() {
    const contentStyle = this.state.fadingOut
      ? { filter: "blur(0.35vw)" }
      : undefined;
    const loadingIndicator = this.state.fadingOut ? (
      &lt;div style={loaderStyle}&gt;-- Loading icon --&lt;/div&gt;
    ) : null;

    return (
      &lt;div className="App" style={{ position: "relative" }}&gt;
        &lt;div style={contentStyle}&gt;
          &lt;div className="top-bar"&gt;
            &lt;div className="title"&gt;.datapoems&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;img className="logo" src="./logo.png" /&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;div className="container"&gt;
            &lt;div className="sloganLineOne"&gt;Poem Theme&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div className="sloganLineTwo"&gt;Detector&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;textarea
              className="inputField"
              placeholder="Please Enter Your Poem Here..."
            /&gt;
            &lt;button className="button" onClick={this.fadeOut}&gt;
              Enter
            &lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;img className="leftTriangle" src="./leftSideTriangle.png" /&gt;
            &lt;img className="rightTriangle" src="./rightSideTriangle.png" /&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        {loadingIndicator}
      &lt;/div&gt;
    );
  }
}

const loaderStyle = {
  position: "absolute", // or position: "fixed"
  top: 0,
  bottom: 0,
  left: 0,
  right: 0,
  display: "flex",
  justifyContent: "center",
  alignItems: "center"
};
</code></pre>

